# Copy to `.env.production`, fill in real values, then encrypt in place:
#
#   bunx @dotenvx/dotenvx encrypt -f .env.production
#
# That rewrites `.env.production` with each value as ciphertext plus a public
# key, which is safe to commit and IS committed — see .gitignore. The matching
# private key is written to `.env.keys`, which must never be committed; add it
# to the repo as the DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY_PRODUCTION secret so CI can decrypt:
#
#   gh secret set DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY_PRODUCTION --repo cwcss/crosswind
#
# The release workflow uses this file only when both it and that secret exist,
# and otherwise falls back to a plain NPM_TOKEN secret.

# npm token used to publish `ts-css`. Publishing a package that does not exist
# yet needs a token that can CREATE packages — an Automation token, or a
# granular token with read/write across all packages. A granular token scoped
# to existing packages returns 404 on the first publish.
NPM_TOKEN=
